  "notes": [
    "Attach-mode world: every address in contracts comes from the upstream repositories' deployment records at the locked commits. Plan steps this config does not list (the ERC-8471 stack, ERC8004Eligibility, IdentityStateEligibility) are deployed from the bundle by foga world deploy, with W as deployer; nothing else is deployed here.",
    "Seam 1: the ARD AgentAdapter is bound to ARD's fixture AIDRegistry (0x36E4...), not to aid-standard's reference instance (0x01C0...). The registry owner key is session-held upstream, so the binding cannot be changed; cells keep their liveness in both registries (8434/AIDRegistry(ard-fixture) is the backing registry).",
    "Seam 2: only AllowlistEligibility is deployed for ERC-8447; the ERC-8004 and identity-state modules are deployed by foga world deploy, the assertion-level and composite modules by the genesis (no owner restriction).",
    "Seam 3: ERC-8471 is deployed upstream at revision 3 while the locked source is revision 4; the two revisions cannot be bound to each other, so FOGA runs its own revision-4 instance here (see upstreamNotAttached) until the upstream revision-4 run lands.",
    "Layer-4 expectations below record the upstream wiring as it is, so a Pass means 'matches the recorded upstream state', not 'matches what FOGA would deploy'.",
    "15 reference contracts the upstream records do not provide at the locked revision are deployed from the bundle by 0x3D177ecaa56402335fC7C6449d35bC1Fa68Bc1b8: 8447/ERC8004Eligibility, 8447/IdentityStateEligibility, 8471/ADRFPolicyRegistry, 8471/ADRFBindingModule, 8471/ADRFFilingModule, 8471/ADRFResolutionModule, 8471/ADRFDecisionModule, 8471/ADRFRecordModule, 8471/ADRFOutcomeModule, 8471/ADRFDisputeRegistry, 8471/DuplicateSettlementVerifier, 8471/DeclaredVersionVerifier, 8471/AttestorQuorumRule, 8471/ADRFACDFBridge, 8471/ADRFServiceEscrow"
  ]
